import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/divides-multiple
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/divides-self
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/divides-sum

theorem cubic-plus-multiple-of-three
  note        By induction on n: (n + 1)³ + 5(n + 1) + 6 is n³ + 5n + 6
              plus 3(n² + n + 2), and 3 divides both parts.
  let n ∈ ℕ₀                                                          (H1)
  then 3 divides n³ + 5n + 6

1.  For all k ∈ ℕ₀, 3 divides k³ + 5k + 6.
    induction on k starting at 0

    base
    1.1.  3 divides 0³ + 5·0 + 6
          arithmetic

    step
    let k ∈ ℕ₀                                                        (K)
    assume step 1 is true for k, the induction hypothesis             (IH)

    1.2.  3 divides 3
          mun:divides-self n := 3

    1.3.  3 divides 3·(k² + k + 2)
          mun:divides-multiple e := 3, a := 3, x := k² + k + 2, from 1.2

    1.4.  3 divides (k³ + 5k + 6) + 3·(k² + k + 2)
          mun:divides-sum d := 3, a := k³ + 5k + 6, b := 3·(k² + k + 2), from IH, 1.3

    1.5.  (k³ + 5k + 6) + 3·(k² + k + 2) = (k + 1)³ + 5(k + 1) + 6
          algebra

    1.6.  3 divides (k + 1)³ + 5(k + 1) + 6
          substitute (k³ + 5k + 6) + 3·(k² + k + 2) = (k + 1)³ + 5(k + 1) + 6 (line 1.5) into line 1.4

2.  3 divides n³ + 5n + 6
    instantiate k := n in line 1
